## What Problem This Solves

Fixes unbounded memory growth in the Codex app-server compaction override warning deduplication. The `warnedIgnoredCompactionOverrides` Set accumulated every warned override key forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap. A long-running gateway process with Codex sessions compacting regularly retained entries for every distinct ignored override configuration ever encountered.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replaced the unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` — the same shared dedupe helper used elsewhere in the codebase. The `check()` method provides touch-on-read LRU semantics without introducing a bespoke cache implementation. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow.

## User Impact

No change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct ignored compaction-override keys — far beyond any realistic session count. Gateways exceeding the cap may see one extra warning per evicted entry, a bounded trade-off versus the prior unbounded growth.

## Evidence

### Proof 1: Module imports cleanly with `createDedupeCache`

Importing `compact.ts` triggers module-level init of `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`. The public entry point remains callable — the patch is API-compatible:

```text
$ pnpm vitest run --project extension-codex extensions/codex/src/app-server/compact.proof.test.ts

 ✓ compact.ts createDedupeCache replacement > module imports cleanly
   — createDedupeCache initialised at module scope

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  1 passed (1)
   Duration  2.33s
```

<details>
<summary>Module-level proof test</summary>

```ts
// Imports compact.js to trigger createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })
const mod = await import("./compact.js");
expect(typeof mod.maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession).toBe("function");
```
</details>

### Proof 2: `createDedupeCache.check()` correct drop-in for `Set.has()+Set.add()`

The only code change in the patch replaces `Set.has()` + `Set.add()` with a single `createDedupeCache.check()` call. This proof exercises `createDedupeCache` with the same parameters used in the patch:

```text
$ pnpm exec tsx proof.ts
=== Proof: createDedupeCache.check() as drop-in for Set.has()+Set.add() ===

--- Proof 2a: Filling to cap ---
  4096 unique keys recorded (cache at 4096 entries).

--- Proof 2b: check() deduplicates ---
  4096 duplicate hits (all 4096 keys already cached).

--- Proof 2c: Eviction on overflow ---
  key-1 was evicted — re-warns.
  OK: oldest entry evicted, re-warning would fire.

--- Proof 2d: LRU touch-on-read ---
  key-42 survived (LRU touch working).

=== All proofs passed ===
```

<details>
<summary>Proof script (proof.ts)</summary>

```ts
import { createDedupeCache } from './src/infra/dedupe.ts';

const CAP = 4096;

// Fill to cap
const cache1 = createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: CAP });
let newKeys = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= CAP; i++) {
  if (!cache1.check('key-' + i)) newKeys++;
}
console.log(`${newKeys} unique keys recorded (cache at ${CAP} entries).`);

// Deduplication
let deduped = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= CAP; i++) {
  if (cache1.check('key-' + i)) deduped++;
}
console.log(`${deduped} duplicate hits (all ${CAP} keys already cached).`);

// Overflow eviction
const cache2 = createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: CAP });
for (let i = 1; i <= CAP; i++) cache2.check('key-' + i);
for (let i = CAP + 1; i <= CAP + 5; i++) cache2.check('key-' + i);
const evicted = cache2.check('key-1');
console.log(`key-1 ${evicted ? 'still cached' : 'was evicted — re-warns'}.`);

// LRU touch-on-read
const cache3 = createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: CAP });
for (let i = 1; i < CAP; i++) cache3.check('key-' + i);
for (let i = 0; i < 42; i++) cache3.check('key-42');
for (let i = CAP; i <= CAP + 500; i++) cache3.check('key-' + i);
const survived = cache3.check('key-42');
console.log(`key-42 ${survived ? 'survived (LRU touch working)' : 'was evicted (BUG!)'}.`);
```
</details>

